From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riched20: TOM formatted text, SetPoint, embedded objects, MoveUp/MoveDown units (6004)

The Text Object Model left GetFormattedText/SetFormattedText, SetPoint and
GetEmbeddedObject (ranges and the selection) as stubs, and MoveUp/MoveDown
took only tomLine (RE-TOM, part 1).

GetFormattedText gives a range over the text; SetFormattedText replaces the
range's text with the other range's text and formatting (its rich text,
streamed out and in; a range of another implementation gives its plain
text), and the range (or selection) then holds the new text. SetPoint makes
an insertion point at a point (screen coordinates, or client ones with
tomClientCoord) or, with Extend, moves the end Type names there.
GetEmbeddedObject gives the object at the start of an insertion point or a
range of the object (S_FALSE and NULL when there is none). MoveUp/MoveDown
also move by tomParagraph (Ctrl+Up/Down; tomExtend extends), tomScreen (Page
Up/Down) and tomWindow (the first or last line in view). Not done: TOM2
(ITextRange2, ITextFont2, ITextPara2, stories, displays).
